# Surgical line-ending pins for a game mod: only the executable text
# surfaces are normalised, leaving data and binary assets to git's own
# detection. bash and shellcheck reject CRLF, so every shell surface
# must be LF on disk - the run-lint / fix-permissions shims under
# scripts/, Gradle's gradlew launcher, and any composite-action scripts
# under .github/. A stray CR on a shebang line otherwise yields
#   env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# on a Linux CI runner.
*.sh    text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# cmd.exe requires CRLF in batch files.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf
